---
import Highlight from '../components/Highlight.astro';
import SignupForm from '../components/SignupForm.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="The Lazy Horseman — a weekly letter about horses"
  description="A weekly letter about horses. One subject, taken apart properly, Thursday mornings, five minutes, sources at the bottom. Written in Shropshire, read in wellingtons."
  hasLocalSignup
>
  <section class="band hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1><span>Hang on,</span><span>why do we</span><span><Highlight>do it</Highlight> that way?</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">A weekly letter about horses. Thursday mornings, five minutes, about as long as the rain takes to pass over.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <button class="btn btn-lg" type="button" data-signup-target="#signup">Get it Thursday</button>
        <a class="squiggle" href="/issues/the-hell-is-a-frog-anyway">Read one first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mud" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </section>

  <div class="band marquee" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="marquee-track">
      <span>The hell is a frog anyway? ✦ Rope halters are worth their weight in hay ✦ The benefits of a track system ✦ Your horse is not cold, you are cold ✦ Everything I got wrong about haynets ✦ Nobody knows what "on the bit" means ✦&nbsp;</span>
      <span>The hell is a frog anyway? ✦ Rope halters are worth their weight in hay ✦ The benefits of a track system ✦ Your horse is not cold, you are cold ✦ Everything I got wrong about haynets ✦ Nobody knows what "on the bit" means ✦&nbsp;</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band cream-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">On the word lazy</p>
          <h2>Lazy is a compliment round here</h2>
          <p>Nobody who keeps horses is lazy. You are up at six in the dark breaking ice out of a trough with the heel of a wellington, and you will do it again tomorrow. Lazy is what comes after that. It is the extra job somebody invented in 1987 that you have quietly stopped doing.</p>
          <p>Most yard wisdom turns up without a receipt. Some of it is excellent and worth knowing why. Working that out takes an evening with the papers open and a tea going cold on the arm of the sofa, and that evening is Thursday morning's newsletter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <div class="card w1" style="transform:rotate(calc(var(--tilt) * -.6deg))">
            <h3>Thursday, five minutes</h3>
            <p>One subject, taken apart properly. It lands at seven, which is about when you are sat in the car deciding whether the ground is too hard.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card w2" style="transform:rotate(calc(var(--tilt) * .5deg))">
            <h3>Mud is the great leveller</h3>
            <p>Every horse in the country is stood in it by November. Whatever the yard cost and whatever the horse cost, somebody is out there at six with a headtorch and a bucket.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card w3" style="transform:rotate(calc(var(--tilt) * -.4deg))">
            <h3>Sources at the bottom, always</h3>
            <p>So you can check my working, or print it off and take it to your vet and have an argument with better ammunition than usual.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band signup" id="signup">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Thursday morning, then.</h2>
      <p>One letter a week, five minutes, sources at the bottom. Something to read in the car park while you wait for the rain to go over.</p>
      <SignupForm id="email-main" />
      <p class="fineprint">Free, and one click to leave. No hard feelings either way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
